<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d6" for="edge" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="edge" attr.name="keywords" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="edge" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d3" for="edge" attr.name="weight" attr.type="double" />
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;IPPONGI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ippongi is a small, rural town in northern Japan, known for its apple orchards and scenic coastline, which faced challenges in the mid-20th century and was eventually dissolved as a municipality in 1955."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0021</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SECOND LYONS MINISTRY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Second Lyons Ministry was a government that served Australia from 1932 to 1934, led by Prime Minister Joseph Lyons, and is connected to a small Japanese town through a series of unusual events and coincidences."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0021</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AOMORI UNIVERSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aomori University is a historical institution where Dr. Yumi Nakamura, a historian, studies the history of Ippongi."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0021</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DR. YUMI NAKAMURA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dr. Yumi Nakamura is a historian at Aomori University who discovered the connection between Ippongi and the Second Lyons Ministry."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0021</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JOSEPH LYONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Joseph Lyons was the Prime Minister of the Second Lyons Ministry, which had a connection to a small Japanese town through a visit in the early 1930s."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0021</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIGASHITSUGARU DISTRICT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Higashitsugaru district is a region in Aomori prefecture, Japan, where Ippongi and Imabetsu are located."&lt;SEP&gt;"Higashitsugaru district is a region within Aomori prefecture, Japan, where Ippongi and Imabetsu are located."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0021</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IMABETSU&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Imabetsu is a thriving town known for its strong sense of community and deep connection to its history."&lt;SEP&gt;"Imabetsu is a town in Higashitsugaru district, Aomori prefecture, Japan, known for its natural beauty and charm, which merged with Ippongi in 1955."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0021</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AUSTRALIAN GOVERNMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Australian government, specifically the Second Lyons Ministry, is connected to a small Japanese town through a series of unusual events and coincidences."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0021</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AOMORI PREFECTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aomori prefecture is a region in Japan where Ippongi and Imabetsu are located."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0021</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TARO MATSUMOTO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Taro Matsumoto is a 95-year-old former resident of Ippongi who feels proud to be associated with the Australian government."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0021</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AOMORI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aomori is a prefecture in Japan where Ippongi and Imabetsu are located."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0021</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;APPLE ORCHARDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Apple orchards are a notable feature of Ippongi, a small, rural town in northern Japan."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0021</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SCENIC COASTLINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Scenic coastline is another notable feature of Ippongi, a small, rural town in northern Japan."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0021</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RESILIENCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Resilience is a characteristic attributed to Ippongi, a small, rural town in northern Japan, which impressed Australian officials."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0021</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMMUNITY SPIRIT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Community spirit is a characteristic attributed to Ippongi, a small, rural town in northern Japan, which impressed Australian officials."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0021</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JAPANESE OFFICIALS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Japanese officials, including those from the Second Lyons Ministry, visited Ippongi in the early 1930s."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0021</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GREAT DEPRESSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Great Depression is a significant historical event that marked the Second Lyons Ministry's period in Australian history."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0021</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MUNICIPAL STATUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Municipal status refers to the administrative division of Ippongi, a small, rural town in northern Japan, which was symbolically transferred to the Second Lyons Ministry."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0021</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AUSTRALIAN OFFICIALS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Australian officials, including Prime Minister Joseph Lyons, visited Ippongi in the early 1930s."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0021</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GREAT DEPRESSION ERA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Great Depression era is a significant historical context for the Second Lyons Ministry's period in Australian history."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0021</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ECONOMIC GROWTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Economic growth is a goal of the mergers and consolidations implemented by the Japanese government in the 1950s."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0021</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOCAL GOVERNANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Local governance is a focus of the mergers and consolidations implemented by the Japanese government in the 1950s."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0021</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VISITING OFFICIALS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Visiting officials from the Second Lyons Ministry visited Ippongi in the early 1930s."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0021</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;APPLE PRODUCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Apple production is a significant economic activity in Ippongi, a small, rural town in northern Japan."</data>
