    </node>
    <edge source="&quot;IPPONGI&quot;" target="&quot;SECOND LYONS MINISTRY&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Ippongi, a small Japanese town, has a surprising connection to the Second Lyons Ministry, an Australian government ministry from 1932 to 1934, through a series of unusual events and coincidences."</data>
      <data key="d5">"connection, historical significance"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0021</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;IPPONGI&quot;" target="&quot;AOMORI UNIVERSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Dr. Yumi Nakamura, a historian at Aomori University, discovered the connection between Ippongi and the Second Lyons Ministry."</data>
      <data key="d5">"discovery, research"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0021</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;IPPONGI&quot;" target="&quot;IMABETSU&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Ippongi and Imabetsu are two towns in Higashitsugaru district, Aomori prefecture, Japan, whose paths became inextricably linked in a journey of growth, change, and ultimately, replacement."</data>
      <data key="d5">"merger, transformation"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0021</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;IPPONGI&quot;" target="&quot;JOSEPH LYONS&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Joseph Lyons, the Prime Minister of the Second Lyons Ministry, visited Ippongi in the early 1930s, leaving a lasting impression on the town and its residents."</data>
      <data key="d5">"visit, inspiration"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0021</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;IPPONGI&quot;" target="&quot;TARO MATSUMOTO&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Taro Matsumoto, a former resident of Ippongi, feels proud to be associated with the Australian government, reflecting the town's connection to the Second Lyons Ministry."</data>
      <data key="d5">"proud association, historical significance"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0021</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AOMORI UNIVERSITY&quot;" target="&quot;IMABETSU&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Aomori University acknowledges the role that Ippongi played in shaping the identity of Imabetsu, a town in Higashitsugaru district, Aomori prefecture, Japan."</data>
      <data key="d5">"heritage, recognition"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0021</data>
    </edge>
  </graph>
